WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.174
This episode focuses on data products.

2
00:00:02.174 --> 00:00:09.667
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:14.796
Detailed tables provide the most variables and include estimates and margins of error.

4
00:00:14.796 --> 00:00:18.195
Subject tables organize selected measures around a topic.

5
00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:23.085
Data profiles summarize characteristics, and comparison profiles emphasize change.

6
00:00:23.085 --> 00:00:26.209
A table identifier communicates product and concept.

7
00:00:26.209 --> 00:00:31.315
Read the title, universe, annotation symbols, and variable labels before downloading.

8
00:00:31.315 --> 00:00:37.623
Filters in data dot census dot gov should be saved or documented so another person can repeat the search.

9
00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:43.367
Profiles are useful for orientation, but a policy claim may require the underlying detailed table.

10
00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:49.345
Export machine-readable data when calculations matter, and preserve an untouched copy of the download.

11
00:00:49.345 --> 00:00:50.695
Torrance application segment.

12
00:00:50.695 --> 00:00:54.000
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

13
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.520
The cited City of Torrance primary source is General Plan, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/Departments-Offices/Departments-Offices/Community-Development/Planning-Division/Comprehensive-Planning/General-Plan.

14
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:11.037
For a local analysis, translate a General Plan question into a documented table search instead of treating a profile as a policy conclusion.

15
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:17.600
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

16
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:27.834
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

17
00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:31.162
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

18
00:01:31.162 --> 00:01:36.060
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

19
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.455
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

20
00:01:40.455 --> 00:01:46.608
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

21
00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:51.066
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
